    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'gesture' (noun) refers specifically to a communicative body movement. While '動作' (dōsa) can encompass such movements, it is a much broader term meaning 'movement,' 'action,' or 'operation' in general, including non-communicative or mechanical movements. For the specific meaning of a communicative 'gesture,' '身振り' (miburi) is a more natural and precise Japanese equivalent for learners.",
